  "facts": [
    "The Thomas J. Hatem Memorial Bridge, opened August 28, 1940, replaced a 13‑foot‑wide, double‑decked 1910 railroad‑converted bridge that had become a bottleneck for trucks and caused frequent side‑swiping accidents.",
    "In 1958 the bridge pioneered exact‑change lanes, and by 1976 introduced AVI decals—large barcode‑like stickers that let vehicles cross automatically, a first for Maryland toll bridges.",
    "Bicycles were barred until July 1, 2016, when the bridge finally opened to them, adding warning lights and later restricting bicycle use to weekends and holidays to protect motorists."
  ],
